    "created_at": "2018-07-10T03:51:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-07-10T03:51:30Z",
    "body": "The first link says that HTML elements, the built-in ones, all have names that are ascii alphanumerics. This doesn't restrict the tagnames of other elements; in particular, custom elements can use non-ASCII characters in their names. These aren't \"HTML elements\", and thus not bound by the statement at that link.  This link also intentionally doesn't go into the gritty details of parsing, as that's what the parser section is for; it just gives you a more general description of how things work that's much easier to read than the actual parser.\r\n\r\nThe second link is the actual parsing algorithm, with all the precise details.",
