    "body": "@tabatkins If I understand you correctly then the **first** rule is common for defined tags by the specification. But you said: _\"This doesn't restrict the tagnames of other elements; in particular, custom elements can use non-ASCII characters in their names. These aren't \"HTML elements\", and thus not bound by the statement at that link.\"_ Why is the **first** rule not suitable for custom elements, they are described by the specification, why not?",
